\ The dip splice must decline when the body's consumed range holds an opaque
\ row: the unresolved-effect `call` collapses the stack to a row_region, and
\ the spliced `+` would reject it (NC.1) where the native dip path compiles
\ `f` with today's row machinery.
\
\ Build-only: the program still cannot build, because the compiled `f` ends
\ row-returning and the entry cannot materialize a row as its result. The
\ golden pins that exact rejection -- the entry's NC.13 -- which is only
\ reachable when `f` itself compiled. A regressed splice fails `f` instead,
\ and the error becomes the compound-fallback inventory.

f: ( q -- ) [ call 5 [ 1 + ] dip drop drop ] ;

[ 7 ] f
